A||N||4||Ferrari355||I have a question about GT & SE tail light wiring harness'!||||4||
Z||000000||Ferrari355||06-05-2000||05:16 PM||||OK, we have an 84 SE and an 86 GT, we are wanting to put the fast back on but are wondering if the wiring harness' are going to plug right up or do you have to change alot of other things? Let me know,<P>     TTYL, Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000001||TOM||06-06-2000||12:41 AM||||I dont about the 84 because weird things are different but you will need to get the wiring harness with the fastback parts. I think there is also a jumper to disconnect.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-06-2000||02:48 AM||||You will need to get the drawings and splice wires in. The harness in 85 thru 88 is totally different than 84. This is the reason that swapping a Fiero 2.8 into an 84 is so difficult. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ferrari355||06-06-2000||04:52 PM||||So do I have to splice it or just swap the Harness'? That sorta confused me, hehe. let me know,<P>           -Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000004||Rodrv6||06-06-2000||08:55 PM||||You are going to have to use the fastback tail light harness and do a LOT of wire splicing to make it work.  If you look carefully at the 84 and compare the routing of the rear harness and where the rear harness plugs into the main car harness with the same thing in the fastback (or any 85-88), you will see big differences in the way the harnesses are run and hooked up.  The 84's were not like any of the newer Fiero's because they were never intended to have the V-6 installed.||||reg||4
